  "body": "As pointed out in #110 its not possible to do `new URLPattern(\"http://[::1]/\")`.  Even if you properly escape the colons like `new URLPattern(\"http://[\\\\:\\\\:1]/\")` it still throws.\r\n\r\nAdding support for this turns out to not be too hard.  The URL spec simply ignores colons inside `[ ]` brackets.  We can do the same in URLPattern.  Of course, for the hostname pattern to be valid the colon's will still need to be escaped.",
